================================================================================
PART 3 -- THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
================================================================================

Shaker (in shaker_py/)
A modified copy of Shaker, by the same research group, redistributed under
the BSD 2-Clause License. See shaker_py/LICENSE for the licence and
shaker_py/NOTICE for the list of modifications made for this study.
Repository : https://github.com/STAR-RG/shaker
Archive : https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5347973
Paper : Silva, Teixeira, and d'Amorim. "Shake It! Detecting Flaky
Tests Caused by Concurrency with Shaker." ICSME 2020.

Ground-truth flaky-test data (in dataset/)
dataset/tests.csv, dataset/flaky.csv, dataset/projects.csv and
dataset/100NOD_manual_classification.csv are DERIVED from the dataset of
Gruber et al., which is licensed CC BY 4.0. They are redistributed here
under the same licence, with attribution, and were produced by filtering
that dataset as documented in analysis/verify_selection.py.
Dataset : Martin Gruber. "Dataset of An Empirical Study of Flaky Tests
in Python." Zenodo, 2021. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4450435
Paper : Gruber, Lukasczyk, Kroiss, and Fraser. "An Empirical Study of
Flaky Tests in Python." ICST 2021, pp. 148-158.

stress-ng
Invoked at runtime as a separate process and installed inside the Docker
image; it is NOT redistributed as part of this artifact. stress-ng is
licensed GPL-2.0. Because it is executed as a separate process rather than
linked, its licence does not extend to the software in this artifact.
https://github.com/ColinIanKing/stress-ng

Subject projects
The Python projects exercised by the experiments are open-source packages
published on PyPI. They are NOT redistributed here: the experiment clones
each one from its own repository at the commit recorded in
dataset/projects.csv, and each remains under its own licence.
